sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila ananassae Turing wavenumber at 2.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila ananassae morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila ananassae specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila ananassae; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics. | D. ananassae is a sequenced ananassae-subgroup species (12 Genomes Consortium 2007); geological age in this slot is 0 Ma. | Ready, Hanson and Benzer (1976) describe the retinal lattice at a scale of a few micrometres. | Gompel et al. (2005) show the biarmipes wing spot is a multi-cell yellow pattern; Wittkopp, Carroll and Kopp (2003) review coarser abdominal pigment.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.11, b=1.15, Dv/Du=19.7 and dx chosen so argmax Re σ(k) equals 2.106 µm. | Diffusivity ratios versus D. americana (139 µm) and D. biarmipes (96 µm) under λ ∝ √D. | Activator field painted as a luminance modulation on the Wikimedia plate.; transfer_boundary: 2.106 µm is this slot's assigned detail-scale wavelength, not a published Turing-wavelength measurement on ananassae cuticle.; does_not_claim: The transverse sex comb and the optomotor-blind chiasma are not claimed as products of this 2.1 µm mode. | The adult body outline is the vendored plate, not an output of the reaction-diffusion field. | Slot 2841's 85 µm power-law parameters were not reused. | The Lean file was not executed by a Lean kernel on this machine.]; phenomenon_size: 348 µm (0.0003476 m, log10=-3.459 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 348 µm to 1.06 m): 348 µm:anas-platyrhynchos-bioelectric-polarity, 1.3 mm:anas-platyrhynchos-vertex-packing, 2.4 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength, 4.4 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-clock-wavefront, 7.1 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-morphogen-condensation, 10.4 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-elastic-buckling, 17.6 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-flux-canalization, 23.3 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(76)90225-6>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0168-9525(03)00194-X>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03235>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06341>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

